# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# A failing public API check writes the current surface beside its approved transcript.
*.received.txt

# The documentation site. docs/_site/ is the built site and docs/api/*.yml the generated API
# reference; both are rebuilt by `dotnet docfx docs/docfx.json` and by docs.yml, and a generated
# directory in version control is a merge conflict waiting for the next doc-comment fix.
# docs/api/index.md is hand-written and stays tracked.
docs/_site/
docs/api/*.yml
docs/api/.manifest

# Credentials. Both OAuth mechanisms take an RSA private key, and this repository's own README tells
# you to make one with `openssl genrsa -out privatekey.pem 3072`. That writes into whatever directory
# you happen to be in, and the repository root is the obvious one — so without these patterns the key
# sits untracked and unignored, one `git add -A` away from being published permanently. Patterns
# first, discipline second: the discipline is what fails at 1am.
#
# `.env.*` as well as `.env`, because the variants (.env.local, .env.development) are the ones
# tooling creates without being asked. `.env.example` stays tracked so a template still works.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
secrets.json
